        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "9486c89f-06c8-3dfe-b010-0f4dc5fd1e12",
                "word": "okapi",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7abdb5ae-262e-463d-bd3f-6659f470fabe",
                        "entry_id": "9486c89f-06c8-3dfe-b010-0f4dc5fd1e12",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "okapis"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e0136bfe-8fcc-30aa-9110-5e8cef2f1af2",
                        "entry_id": "9486c89f-06c8-3dfe-b010-0f4dc5fd1e12",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce de ruminant des forêts équatoriales de l’Afrique centrale, de la même famille que la girafe, plus petit et qui a des zébrures noires et blanches sur les pattes et l’arrière train."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "41ab51a0-da9f-439b-b0d9-d053a42de733",
                                "sense_id": "e0136bfe-8fcc-30aa-9110-5e8cef2f1af2",
                                "text": "L’okapi se reconnaît à ses pattes rayées comme un zèbre et à son allure de girafe sans tache et au petit cou."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "31efb698-cf91-44c0-bf4a-e3b7a32715a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "9486c89f-06c8-3dfe-b010-0f4dc5fd1e12",
                        "source_sense_id": "e0136bfe-8fcc-30aa-9110-5e8cef2f1af2",
                        "target_lang_word": "Okapi",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Okapi",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3bbae079-9a9c-3389-820a-eba992434973",
                                        "entry_id": "5dc626a9-87b7-3a28-b2a2-74821cea94b7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "kurzhalsige, dunkelbraune Giraffe mit weißen Querstreifen an den Oberschenkeln"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4e98304-c559-4e60-89c5-5128b642eb6c",
                                                "sense_id": "3bbae079-9a9c-3389-820a-eba992434973",
                                                "text": "Das Okapi kommt in der Natur einzig in der Demokratischen Republik Kongo vor."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8584ab6c-4eae-453b-be89-025d4e1e1a72",
                        "source_entry_id": "9486c89f-06c8-3dfe-b010-0f4dc5fd1e12",
                        "source_sense_id": "e0136bfe-8fcc-30aa-9110-5e8cef2f1af2",
                        "target_lang_word": "okapi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "okapi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efb388e1-23dd-3abb-a431-722c22fb8d15",
                                        "entry_id": "ebc781fa-124d-3839-8708-707f0c8f4c6d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large ruminant mammal, of species Okapia johnstoni, found in the rainforests of the Congo, related to the giraffe but with a much shorter neck, a reddish-brown coat, and zebra-like stripes on the hindquarters."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d6dc3ec-cc14-457b-b884-95b8bb0f8477",
                                                "sense_id": "efb388e1-23dd-3abb-a431-722c22fb8d15",
                                                "text": "Personally I esteem it a more fascinating and a more important task to investigate the relations of the Okapi with the Giraffe on the one hand, and its fossil relatives on the other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffbbb1ad-70ea-412c-aeab-7ea933dc173c",
                                                "sense_id": "efb388e1-23dd-3abb-a431-722c22fb8d15",
                                                "text": "[page 498, column 1] [I]n leading them [African Pygmies] back to the forests where they dwelt, I obtained much information from them on the subject of the horse-like animal which they called the \"Okapi.\" […] [page 499, column 1] The coloration of the Okapi is quite extraordinary. […] The hind quarters, hind and fore legs are either snowy white or pale cream color, touched here and there with orange. They are boldly marked, however, with purple-black stripes and splodges, which give that zebra-like appearance to the limbs of the Okapi that caused the first imperfect account of it to indicate the discovery of a new striped horse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b8b62a5-01e3-4ee6-a31c-5b62dfe3ffa5",
                                                "sense_id": "efb388e1-23dd-3abb-a431-722c22fb8d15",
                                                "text": "[O]ne day I quite modestly gave the dimensions of an okapi I had shot in the Lincolnshire fens. The Major turned a beautiful Tyrian scarlet (I remember thinking at the time that I should like my bathroom hung in that colour), and I think that at that moment he almost found it in his heart to dislike me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "172efe8f-cc7c-4a0d-99e8-837176d9ff1d",
                                                "sense_id": "efb388e1-23dd-3abb-a431-722c22fb8d15",
                                                "text": "Dr. [Cuthbert] Christy adds his testimony to that of his predecessors in the same quest as to the \"invisibility\" of the okapi, whose markings and coloration—pace Colonel Theodore Roosevelt—so break up the surface of its large body and long legs as to cause it to fuse with the dark-brown, russet, while and yellow-white of the twigs and stems and leaf-stalks amongst which it moves. He also points out that the hoofs of the okapi are so closely pressed together that the footprint is almost like that of the single-toed donkey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b9cc5b5-1b06-4898-9a6c-dbafdb7ec6b6",
                                                "sense_id": "efb388e1-23dd-3abb-a431-722c22fb8d15",
                                                "text": "I also took out a licence to shoot small game, costing fifty francs, which can be obtained on the spot, and under which I was able to shoot all kinds of game, excepting elephants, chimpanzis, gorillas and okapis."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
